<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Acre</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Acre is a port city on the coast of present-day northern Israel. In the era of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusades</a> it was a major <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader</a> stronghold and trading centre, taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> in 1187 and recaptured during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a>, which made it central to the conflicts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a>. Its capture by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a> in 1291 ended the Crusader presence in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>.</p></div>
